{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויירא יעקב", :translit "vayyira ya'akov", :gloss "and Jacob feared"} {:he "והיה זרעך כעפר הארץ", :translit "vehayah zar'akh ke'afar ha'aretz", :gloss "and your seed shall be as the dust of the earth"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Logical inference: the plural form of the divine promise allows fulfillment through future offspring, leaving room for fear regarding the existing children."}], :frame {:text "Jacob was promised 'and your seed shall be as the dust of the earth' (Genesis 28:14). Since 'seed' is a collective noun used in the plural, the promise could theoretically be fulfilled through children not yet born, leaving room for genuine fear that his current children — specifically the family traveling with him — might be imperiled.", :sources ["Genesis 28:14"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Logical inference: the plural form of the divine promise allows fulfillment through future offspring, leaving room for fear regarding the existing children.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:09:30.628104412Z", :model "glm-5.2"}